      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree 76810a0e47ffb1ef17b5182ccf7398e6ce440541\nparent 22245aedf4000e62b597d40091a23388f2fa533a\nauthor Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1791674019 +0200\ncommitter Ferdinando Ametrano <ferdinando@ametrano.net> 1791880000 +0200\n\nmusig: Clear secrets before ARG_CHECK failures in partial_sign\n\nsecp256k1_musig_partial_sign loads the secnonce scalars into stack\nvariables and zeroes the secnonce, so those copies are the only ones\nleft. The ARG_CHECKs after that point return without calling\nsecp256k1_musig_partial_sign_clear, which leaves the secrets on the\nstack.\n\nMove the NULL checks before the secnonce is loaded. The check that the\nsecnonce matches the keypair needs both loaded, so clear the secrets\nbefore it fails. Its condition is repeated rather than stored so that\nthe ARG_CHECK message keeps the expression.\n",
