      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "Thanks @real-or-random, done in 986d6ad (force-pushed): the NULL checks now come before the secnonce is loaded, so a call with a NULL argument leaves the secnonce as is and produces no signature. The key-match check needs both the secnonce and the keypair loaded, so it still clears the secrets before it fails. The header says the function \"overwrites the given secnonce with zeros\"; should it note the NULL case?\n\n@Yudis-bit, the head changed: could you re-test 986d6ad and renew your ACK if it still holds?\n",
